Z||000000||fropuff||04-01-2001||11:42 PM||||Hey there.  I thought I might let you guys know what I plan to do to the GT this spring/summer.  I was going to go with a 3.4, but it would be ~$2500, and I want to buy a winter car this fall.  Anyway, here we go...<BR>New crap to buy:<BR>1)Front Fascia<BR>2)Windshield<BR>3)Radio Pod Fascia<BR>4)Right Side Front Marker Light<BR>5)Dew Wipes<BR>6)Right Side Drip Rail<BR>7)Side Scoop (like DXRs; gotta see it!)<BR>8)Headliner<BR>9)Tinted GT Sail Panels<BR>10)Leather Seats (?)<P>Crap to do:<BR>1)Paint front fascia, side scoop & quarter panel, wheels, ground FX, black trim/moulding<BR>2)Polish rail lamp lenses, plastic gauge covers<BR>3)Buff entire car.<P>That's my list, so far.  Let's hear what yours is.  Thanks.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||04-01-2001||11:46 PM||||Paint, Paint and ummmm Paint <P>You look like you have a lot of work on your hands, what are you doing fooling around on the forum GET BUSY! hehe<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000002||fropuff||04-01-2001||11:51 PM||||Well, I won't paint the panels myself.  I will, however, paint the black parts (engine grilles, mirrors, moulding, etc) myself.  I'll leave the other painting to the paint guy.  I do have a project on my hands!  Let's hear your projects!  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
