Z||000004||Kelvin Vivian||04-02-2001||06:38 AM||||For the GT:<P>1) Have the rear decklid repainted. It's starting to go on me.<BR>2) Have the leather seats restored.<BR>3) new belts and hoses in the engine compartment.<BR>4) needs new t-top roof seals. Perhaps new t-tops too, but current ones are in decent "daily driver" condition.<BR>5) shampoo interior as previous owner was a heavy smoker...<BR>6) solve all electric bugs, and replace turn signal stalk/cruise control because the cruise control wire has been snipped (also by previous owner) <P>For the 87 SE:<P>1) have tranny leak sealed.<BR>2) have front facia and lower body trim repainted.<P>In general:<BR> <BR>1) go on bi-monthly trips to Pick-N-Pull yards to find Fiero treasures...<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=1&res=high">  88 T-top, 5-spd & 87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||04-02-2001||09:37 AM||||Well.. for the 84 the plan is to get it running  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>For my 86 GT..<BR>New decklid, ground f/x<BR>Pull the engine, do some head work if the oil pressure is still good, if not rebuild it<BR>New shocks/struts<BR>New tires<BR>Possibly lowering springs<BR>and whatever else I have the money for..||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||04-02-2001||10:50 AM||||hmmm...mainly scratch my head and wonder what to do first and now to pay for it. the major things i canthink of off hand.<P>'87 coupe: waiting for chin spoiler delivery to try grafting to gt nose and installation.<P>gt rear that i may try to alter or just install as is.<P>various stereo repairs and reconfiguring (the dealer says they may finaly get my subs in)<P>indy: headwork on the engine. possibly at whatever time i try it put the header i have on it. as much refurbishing as i can. i try not to make plans to change it but i would like an indyscoop,maybe an inobtrusive stereo system and more wheels. stuff  can change back if i want.<P>'84 cheap thrill: brake job and see if i can figure out what drains the battery. not sure beyond that.<P>'84 chop top: if you've seen the million and one off the wall questions, they're mainly for this car. no set plans.<P>they could all use paint jobs, and i'm keeping an eye out and researching engine swaps. i'd like to try at least one. in dreams i'd swap them all (maybe not the indy, unless i stumbled over a superduty and knew what to do with it).   ||||reg||1
