Z||000017||fropuff||04-11-2001||02:39 PM||||Well, I've changed my mind on the engine again.  I was going to go with the 3800 S/C, but chatting with Black88GT last night, I've decided to go with the 3.4 pushrod again.  Much cheaper, and I can do it myself, I believe.  Anyway, I've done a little rough estimating on the cost of my project, minus the engine, and here's the totals: <P>-$160.00 for the front fascia<BR>-$0 for the windshield (insurance   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  )<BR>-$20.00 for the radio pod fascia<BR>-$20.00 for the marker light<BR>-$50.00 for the dew wipes<BR>-$50.00 for the driprail<BR>-$0 for the scoop (changed my mind)<BR>-$35 for a headliner kit<BR>-$200 for tinted sail panels<BR>-$500 for paint/labor<BR>-$40 for paint/sandpaper for black items<BR>-$5.00 for plastic polish<BR>-$25.00 for polish, wax, etc.<P>Total: $1105 <P>These aren't exact; I guess I can cut a little here and there.  Anyway, a budget of $1100 is about right.  The GT will pretty much be complete after this.  Besides the performance stuff of course.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||Coop88||04-11-2001||11:01 PM||||For my formula:<P>-Poly bushings front/rear<BR>-factory sunroof (needs paint)<BR>-headliner<BR>-replace passenger doorskin<BR>-8" sub under the dash somehow (probably will ditch the other factory speakers too)<BR>-do something to the exhaust to get rid of that "drone" I hear at about 2k rpms(gives me a headache on long trips)<BR>-make another attempt to eliminate the creaking from my front brakes(embarassing), fix that parking brake<BR>-hunt down that funny snapping noise I hear inside my car when I hit a bump(It's soooo annoying...)might be the rear glass, I've removed everything else<BR>-leather seats-maybe<P>That's about it. My car will be in the garage for awhile. <P>||||reg||10
