Z||000026||Taijiguy||05-20-2001||08:20 AM||||*sigh* I wish I hadn't seen this thread....now I'm thinking of all the hoorah I need to do...<P><LI>Oil change (Syntech, what else. $$)<BR><LI>New cap, rotor, and maybe plugs<BR><LI>Fix small crack in manifold before it becomes a big crack<BR><LI>Poly front control arm bushings<BR><LI>Poly cradle bushings<BR><LI>All new sway bar bushings front and rear<BR><LI>4 wheel alignment<BR><LI>Finish body work and mods<BR><LI>Paint, paint, and paint some more<BR><LI>Install new fuel pressure, vacuum, volt, and air/fuel ratio gauges<BR><LI>Fine tune carb and maybe play with cam timing<BR><LI>New (hopefully)true dual exhaust system<BR><LI>New interior w/ Mr.Mikes leather and heaters<BR><LI>Maybe new stereo head unit<BR><LI>Install sub<BR><LI>Oh yeah, have to work once in a while to make money to finance all this stuff too<BR><LI>Wish I had just spent all that money on a new car...<P>(why do I suddenly feel less than completely sane...?)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000027||trigger||05-20-2001||10:18 AM||||Haze: I love those 17" wheels you have on the SE now.  Don't know why you would get rid of them.<P>For my 88 coupe auto:<P>-Do something with the shift kit sitting in the corner of my room<P>*-Install factory sunroof, 1996 Eclipse GST spoiler, left vent panel<P>-Paint previous items<P>*-Have windshield installed<P>-CD player, 1500 watt power akoustic amp, two 10" subs, new 4x10 speakers for front<P>-Really clean interior<P>-Get side scoops(maybe like Fiero5 has, or Tigger's side scoop)<P>-Possibly buy the really cheap 87 coupe, 5speed my mechanic in Ryan has<P>-Poly bushings everywhere, lower it, rims-tires, Formula rear swaybar<P>-Keep dreaming of where I'll get the money for all of this.  I just paid off the car on Friday, May 18.<P>* means I already ordered the parts.  Thanks mrfiero<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000028||Dave Gunsul||05-20-2001||05:13 PM||||I'm waiting for two things; first for the engine shop to finish my new engine and secound for fropuff to change his mind again....and again.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000029||fropuff||05-20-2001||05:36 PM||||Well Dave, you'll be happy to hear that I have indeed changed my mind again.  Not on the performance aspect, but on my choice for appearance.  I have decided to make the '86 GT an '88 GT "clone".  I will paint the ground effects red and the wheels black.  Here is my new updated list... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Things needed:<P>-Radio pod fascia<BR>-Right side front marker light<BR>-Dew wipes (doing them next weekend)<BR>-Right side drip rail<BR>-Headliner<BR>-Tinted GT sail panels<P>Things wanted:<P>-Center console w/ sub (from AusFiero)<BR>-Pioneer DEH-P47DH 1.5 DIN CD player <BR>-Infinity Kappa/Reference 4"x6" plate speakers<BR>-Bass blockers for all 6 speakers<BR>-Power pulley kit (Fiero Store)<BR>-Performance auto shift kit (Fiero Store)<BR>-Cold air intake (Chris West)<P>Things to do:<P>-Paint front fascia, ground FX red<BR>-Sand and paint wheel centers black<BR>-Paint engine grilles w/ high temp. paint<BR>-Buff <BR>-Have steering wheel recovered<P>I think I still am going to stick with the 3.4L pushrod idea.  Before I do that, I'm going to get a nitrous kit.  I don't go fast anymore that I've gotten a ticket, but I really like to street race (to a reasonable distance/MPH).  I've only got one defeat and six kills so far.  The defeat was a 1993 Nissan Maxima.  That time, I didn't manually shift the auto trans.  This seems to help a lot.  Here's the kills:  Jeep Cherokee, Chev Blazer, Ford Taurus station wagon, Grand Prix, Dodge Neon, Chev S-10.  I actually raced the wagon and the GP.  The others, they took off like a BOOH and I took off normally.  I wait until they reach the door, then I let em have it.  If I had nitrous, I could keep up with the big dogs ('Vettes, muscle cars, etc.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||10
Z||000030||Dave Gunsul||05-20-2001||10:36 PM||||I know I'll probably take heat for this but I would still advise against using NOS, especially on the street and frequently in a <BR>stock engine.<BR>You will end up buying a new engine sooner than you think.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000031||fropuff||05-20-2001||11:06 PM||||Well, if you don't like me changing my mind so much, why did you say that, you bastard??!?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I've talked with many people with nitrous, and I have outweighed the good and bad.  When I do get a kit, I plan on going with an approximate HP shot of 40-50.  This seems to be quite a bit, but in reality is not.  I do plan on upgrading the fuel and ignition sysytems as well.  I would go to a higher HP output when I'm on the strip too.  My engine has 64K on it, and I'd get an engine before anything major could go wrong.  I won't even do it until next summer anyway.  I plan on having enough $ to buy a 3.4L pushrod anyway.  If I have quite a bit, I might go with a 3.4L turbocharged.  How's that for indecisiveness?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000032||Dave Gunsul||05-21-2001||09:52 PM||||Don't worry about me Fropuff I was just pokin' fun at you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I too went back and forth on what combo to go with, now if the engine shop would just finish the damned thing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Even though NOS is hard to beat, if not impossible, for bang for the buck it is very hard on your engine especially if used a LOT<BR>on a STOCK engine. It's also very impractical for the occasional stop light wars. <BR>Just a thought.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||7
